        class="inline-flex h-7 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md px-2 text-xs font-medium text-text-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-surface-raised hover:text-text-primary focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary"
        type="button"
      >
        <span
          aria-hidden="true"
          class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]"
        >
          content_copy
        </span>
        Copy
      </button>
      <span
        class="sr-only"
        role="status"
      />
    </div>
    <pre
      class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-3.5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.65] text-text-primary focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary focus-visible:outline-offset-[-2px]"
      tabindex="0"
    >
      <code>
        tar -czf my-awesome-game-1.0.0.tgz -C bundle .
      </code>
    </pre>
  </div>
  <p
    class="my-4"
  >
    The tarball must contain 
    <code
      class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
    >
      index.js
    </code>
     at the root level (no 
    <code
      class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
    >
      package/
    </code>
    
wrapper); the installer refuses it otherwise. Verify:
  </p>
  <div
    class="my-5 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-container"
    data-code-block="true"
  >
    <div
      class="flex min-h-9 items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-border-subtle/70 py-1 pl-4 pr-1.5"
    >
      <span
        class="font-mono text-xs text-text-muted"
      >
        Shell
      </span>
      <button
        aria-label="Copy code"
        class="inline-flex h-7 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md px-2 text-xs font-medium text-text-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-surface-raised hover:text-text-primary focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary"
        type="button"
      >
        <span
          aria-hidden="true"
          class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]"
        >
          content_copy
        </span>
        Copy
      </button>
      <span
        class="sr-only"
        role="status"
      />
    </div>
    <pre
      class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-3.5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.65] text-text-primary focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary focus-visible:outline-offset-[-2px]"
      tabindex="0"
    >
      <code>
        tar tzf my-awesome-game-1.0.0.tgz | head -5
# Should show: ./ and ./index.js
      </code>
    </pre>
  </div>
  <h2
    class="group scroll-mt-24 mt-14 border-t border-border-subtle/60 pt-8 text-[24px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em] text-text-primary sm:text-[27px]"
    id="step-4--publish-the-tarball"
  >
    Step 4 — Publish the tarball
    <a
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="ml-2 font-normal text-text-muted no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity hover:text-primary group-hover:opacity-100"
      href="#step-4--publish-the-tarball"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      #
    </a>
  </h2>
  <p
    class="my-4"
  >
    Host the 
    <code
      class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
    >
      .tgz
    </code>
     file somewhere publicly accessible:
  </p>
  <ul
    class="list-disc my-4 space-y-1 pl-6 marker:text-text-muted"
  >
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <p
        class="my-2.5"
      >
        <strong
          class="font-semibold text-text-primary"
        >
          GitHub Releases
        </strong>
         (free, versioned, CDN-backed):
      </p>
      <div
        class="my-5 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-container"
        data-code-block="true"
      >
        <div
          class="flex min-h-9 items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-border-subtle/70 py-1 pl-4 pr-1.5"
        >
          <span
            class="font-mono text-xs text-text-muted"
          >
            Shell
          </span>
          <button
            aria-label="Copy code"
            class="inline-flex h-7 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md px-2 text-xs font-medium text-text-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-surface-raised hover:text-text-primary focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary"
            type="button"
          >
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]"
            >
              content_copy
            </span>
            Copy
          </button>
          <span
            class="sr-only"
            role="status"
          />
        </div>
        <pre
          class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-3.5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.65] text-text-primary focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary focus-visible:outline-offset-[-2px]"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          <code>
            gh release create v1.0.0 my-awesome-game-1.0.0.tgz
          </code>
        </pre>
      </div>
      <p
        class="my-2.5"
      >
        URL: 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          https://github.com/you/my-awesome-game/releases/download/v1.0.0/my-awesome-game-1.0.0.tgz
        </code>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <p
        class="my-2.5"
      >
        <strong
          class="font-semibold text-text-primary"
        >
          npm
        </strong>
         (if you prefer): 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          npm publish
        </code>
         → URL becomes the tarball download.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <p
        class="my-2.5"
      >
        <strong
          class="font-semibold text-text-primary"
        >
          Your own CDN / S3 / object storage
        </strong>
        .
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2
    class="group scroll-mt-24 mt-14 border-t border-border-subtle/60 pt-8 text-[24px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em] text-text-primary sm:text-[27px]"
    id="step-5--submit-to-the-marketplace"
  >
    Step 5 — Submit to the marketplace
    <a
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="ml-2 font-normal text-text-muted no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity hover:text-primary group-hover:opacity-100"
      href="#step-5--submit-to-the-marketplace"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      #
    </a>
  </h2>
  <p
    class="my-4"
  >
    On the instance that will run the plugin (the catalog is per instance),
as any signed-in user:
  </p>
  <div
    class="my-5 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface-container"
    data-code-block="true"
  >
    <div
      class="flex min-h-9 items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-border-subtle/70 py-1 pl-4 pr-1.5"
    >
      <span
        class="font-mono text-xs text-text-muted"
      >
        Shell
      </span>
      <button
        aria-label="Copy code"
        class="inline-flex h-7 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md px-2 text-xs font-medium text-text-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-surface-raised hover:text-text-primary focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary"
        type="button"
      >
        <span
          aria-hidden="true"
          class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]"
        >
          content_copy
        </span>
        Copy
      </button>
      <span
        class="sr-only"
        role="status"
      />
    </div>
    <pre
      class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-3.5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.65] text-text-primary focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary focus-visible:outline-offset-[-2px]"
      tabindex="0"
    >
      <code>
        curl -X POST https://chat.example.com/api/marketplace/submit \\
  -H "Origin: https://chat.example.com" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -H "Cookie: lf_guest=..." \\
  -d '{
    "pluginId": "my-awesome-game",
    "name": "My Awesome Game",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "type": "game",
    "publisher": "Your Name",
    "summary": "A fast-paced word guessing game.",
    "category": "game",
    "tags": ["word", "party"],
    "permissions": ["create_game_session"],
    "manifestUrl": "https://github.com/you/my-awesome-game/releases/download/v1.0.0/my-awesome-game-1.0.0.tgz",
    "requiresVoiceRoom": true
  }'
      </code>
    </pre>
  </div>
  <p
    class="my-4"
  >
    There is no submit form; use the API.
  </p>
  <h2
    class="group scroll-mt-24 mt-14 border-t border-border-subtle/60 pt-8 text-[24px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em] text-text-primary sm:text-[27px]"
    id="step-6--admin-review"
  >
    Step 6 — Admin review
    <a
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="ml-2 font-normal text-text-muted no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity hover:text-primary group-hover:opacity-100"
      href="#step-6--admin-review"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      #
    </a>
  </h2>
  <p
    class="my-4"
  >
    Your submission enters the review queue with 
    <code
      class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
    >
      reviewStatus: 'pending'
    </code>
    .
The instance owner reviews it at 
    <code
      class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
    >
      /admin/moderation
    </code>
    :
  </p>
  <ul
    class="list-disc my-4 space-y-1.5 pl-6 marker:text-text-muted"
  >
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        <strong
          class="font-semibold text-text-primary"
        >
          Approve
        </strong>
         → the server downloads the tarball and pins its SHA-256 and
size; the plugin appears on that instance's 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          /marketplace
        </code>
         page.
      </span>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        <strong
          class="font-semibold text-text-primary"
        >
          Reject
        </strong>
         → you get feedback and can resubmit.
      </span>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p
    class="my-4"
  >
    Once approved, the instance owner can (with

    <code
      class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
    >
      LOBBYFORGE_DYNAMIC_PLUGINS_ENABLED=true
    </code>
    ):
  </p>
  <ol
    class="list-decimal my-4 space-y-1.5 pl-6 marker:text-text-muted"
  >
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        Browse it at 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          /marketplace
        </code>
        .
      </span>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        Click 
        <strong
          class="font-semibold text-text-primary"
        >
          Install
        </strong>
         → the server downloads the tarball again, checks it
against the pinned digest, extracts it to

        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          &lt;LOBBYFORGE_PLUGIN_INSTALL_DIR&gt;/&lt;pluginId&gt;/&lt;version&gt;/
        </code>
         (compose sets

        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          /app/plugins/installed
        </code>
        , on the volume the plugin-worker mounts
read-only), has the worker load that exact version and only then
records it as the active one.
      </span>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        Enable it per server with 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          POST /api/servers/{id}/apps
        </code>
        

        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          {"pluginId":"…","enabled":true}
        </code>
        . The Apps panel and the activity
picker list compiled-in plugins only.
      </span>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <h2
    class="group scroll-mt-24 mt-14 border-t border-border-subtle/60 pt-8 text-[24px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em] text-text-primary sm:text-[27px]"
    id="versioning--updates"
  >
    Versioning & updates
    <a
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="ml-2 font-normal text-text-muted no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity hover:text-primary group-hover:opacity-100"
      href="#versioning--updates"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      #
    </a>
  </h2>
  <p
    class="my-4"
  >
    To release a new version:
  </p>
  <ol
    class="list-decimal my-4 space-y-1.5 pl-6 marker:text-text-muted"
  >
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        Bump 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          version
        </code>
         in your plugin's 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          manifest
        </code>
         and 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          package.json
        </code>
        .
      </span>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        Build + tarball + publish the new version.
      </span>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        Re-submit to the marketplace with the same 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          pluginId
        </code>
         but new 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          version
        </code>
      </span>
      <ul
        class="list-disc my-2 space-y-1.5 pl-6 marker:text-text-muted"
      >
        <li
          class="pl-1"
        >
          <span>
            updated 
            <code
              class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
            >
              manifestUrl
            </code>
            . The catalog entry is updated and goes back to

            <code
              class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
            >
              pending
            </code>
            : it must be approved again (which pins the new bundle)
before it can be installed.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p
    class="my-4"
  >
    Installing the new version extracts it next to the old one. The old
version keeps running until the worker has loaded the new one; then the
old folder is deleted. If the worker refuses the new bundle, the old
version stays active. The active version and a digest of its files are
recorded in 
    <code
      class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
    >
      &lt;pluginId&gt;/active.json
    </code>
    , and every worker call names that
exact version — the worker refuses anything else. Running sessions carry
on with the new reducer, and their saved state goes through your

    <code
      class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
    >
      migrateState
    </code>
     first, so version your state.
  </p>
  <h2
    class="group scroll-mt-24 mt-14 border-t border-border-subtle/60 pt-8 text-[24px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em] text-text-primary sm:text-[27px]"
    id="security-notes"
  >
    Security notes
    <a
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="ml-2 font-normal text-text-muted no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity hover:text-primary group-hover:opacity-100"
      href="#security-notes"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      #
    </a>
  </h2>
  <ul
    class="list-disc my-4 space-y-1.5 pl-6 marker:text-text-muted"
  >
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        Your bundle runs 
        <strong
          class="font-semibold text-text-primary"
        >
          server-side only
        </strong>
        , in the isolated 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          plugin-worker
        </code>
        
container: a fresh child process per call with an empty environment, a
128 MB heap and a 10 s budget, no host secrets, a read-only plugin
directory and an internal network only. Your panel is not rendered
(ADR-002). The worker is built for 
        <strong
          class="font-semibold text-text-primary"
        >
          reviewed
        </strong>
         code, not hostile code
(ADR-001), so expect the instance owner to read your bundle.
      </span>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        The host turns a crash or timeout in your code into a failed request,
so it won't take down the API, but you should still test thoroughly.
      </span>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          ctx.storage
        </code>
         reaches the host's database through a short-lived
capability scoped to one community and your plugin.
      </span>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        Do not import 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          @lobbyforge/db
        </code>
        , 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          ioredis
        </code>
        , 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          postgres
        </code>
        , or any Node-only
module — your plugin should be a pure reducer + React component.
      </span>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pl-1"
    >
      <span>
        The 
        <code
          class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
        >
          permissions
        </code>
         array in your manifest declares what your plugin can
do. Be honest — overstating permissions may delay review.
      </span>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2
    class="group scroll-mt-24 mt-14 border-t border-border-subtle/60 pt-8 text-[24px] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em] text-text-primary sm:text-[27px]"
    id="template"
  >
    Template
    <a
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="ml-2 font-normal text-text-muted no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity hover:text-primary group-hover:opacity-100"
      href="#template"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      #
    </a>
  </h2>
  <p
    class="my-4"
  >
    A starter repo is planned at 
    <code
      class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
    >
      github.com/lobbyforge/plugin-template
    </code>
    . For
now, copy 
    <code
      class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.86em] text-text-primary"
    >
      plugins/hushle/
    </code>
     as a reference — it's a complete, shipping
example.
  </p>
</div>
`;
